.TH BINARYWHY 1
.SH NAME
binarywhy \\- inspect executable metadata and content identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B binarywhy
binarywhy --path EXECUTABLE [--format json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Produces a JSON executable metadata and SHA-256 identity observation. It does not establish provenance or trust.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBbinarywhy --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
